                "To quantitatively govern cannibalization, corporate marketing controllers utilize Cross-Price Elasticity of Demand (CPE) and the Cannibalization Rate (CR). The cannibalization rate measures the percentage of unit sales generated by the new product that would have otherwise been captured by the firm's existing offerings. Mathematically, the Cannibalization Rate is expressed as: Cannibalization Rate = (Lost Unit Sales of Existing Products) / (Total Unit Sales of New Product). If a company launches a new flanker product selling one hundred thousand units, but seventy thousand of those units represent customers switching away from its existing flagship line, the cannibalization rate is an alarming seventy percent.",
